    "title": "Vikings Trying To Stay Perfect - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Learfield Wire Services ,\n21 hours ago (Tampa Bay, FL) -- The Vikings will put their perfect start to the season on the line Sunday when they take on the winless Bucs. Starting quarterback Kyler Murray has been announced as the starter. He won the job out of training camp but was knocked out of the Packers game in the opener and also missed last weeks trip to Chicago. Even though the Vikes won both games under Carson Wentz, Murray is back as the number one guy and will try and hand the Bucs a third straight loss. Kick off tomorrow afternoon is at 3:05 P-M. Read full article",
